Stonewick was a real place once. Thirty-odd years back, a dry-summer
fire got loose in the granary district -- the Long Burn, scavengers
still call it -- and killed enough people that the garrison never
built its numbers back up. Within a few years everyone who could
leave had. What's left is picked over by scavengers, deserters, and
whatever's since moved into the flooded cellars and rotten granary
lofts.

You're arriving at the gatehouse on the old east wall, same as anyone
else who's ever wandered in.

Commands you can actually run here:
  say <text>     speak to everyone in your room
  who            list connected players
  eval <code>    compile and run one LPC statement, e.g.
                 eval return 1 + 1;
  help           show this list again
  quit           save and disconnect
  shutdown       stop the whole driver process

Movement (each room's own description lists its real exits):
  north / south / east / west

Talking to people:
  talk <name>              start a conversation
  talk <name> about <topic> ask about something specific

Once you are holding the reeve's rod (left on the gatehouse's own
requisition desk, and handed to you automatically when you arrive):
  clone <path>   requisition a copy of an existing design into this
                 room or your pack
  purge <name>   clear away an unwanted object in the room
  create <name>  cobble together something new from raw salvage
